  "id": "Compound::DB01023 - Gene::5153",
  "verbalization": "Felodipine, a dihydropyridine calcium channel blocker, is directly linked to Pde1b through a shared biological pathway. The evidence suggests that Felodipine, as part of the dihydropyridine class, binds to Pde1b, which is a key enzyme involved in the regulation of vascular tone and blood pressure. This relationship is supported by the hierarchical inclusion of Felodipine within the dihydropyridine family and its inclusion in the calcium channel antagonists group, which in turn includes Nicardipine. The binding of Nicardipine to Pde1b is a recurring mechanism across both paths, reinforcing the role of Pde1b in the pharmacological action of these compounds. The integration of these pathways highlights a consistent mechanism by which Felodipine influences Pde1b, suggesting a broader functional relationship in the context of cardiovascular regulation.",
